WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.141
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:09.675
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:18.038
Unit twenty-nine: Past Simple Questions and Negatives. Today you will ask and answer questions about the past with did and didn't.

4
00:00:18.338 --> 00:00:20.944
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.388
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:26.868
Did.

7
00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:30.545
Did means the helping verb for past questions.

8
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.499
Did you eat breakfast?

9
00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:35.620
Your turn. Say: Did.

10
00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:39.189
Did.

11
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:40.638
Didn't.

12
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.104
Didn't means did not.

13
00:00:43.717 --> 00:00:45.124
I didn't go to school.

14
00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:48.427
Your turn. Say: Didn't.

15
00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:52.128
Didn't.

16
00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:53.606
Did you...?.

17
00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:57.257
Did you...? means a question about the past.

18
00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.269
Did you watch TV?

19
00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:02.002
Your turn. Say: Did you...?.

20
00:01:04.867 --> 00:01:05.659
Did you...?.

21
00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:07.650
Yes, I did.

22
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.068
Yes, I did means a short positive answer.

23
00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:13.929
Did you call him? Yes, I did.

24
00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:17.332
Your turn. Say: Yes, I did.

25
00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.679
Yes, I did.

26
00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:23.708
No, I didn't.

27
00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.030
No, I didn't means a short negative answer.

28
00:01:27.617 --> 00:01:29.886
Did you see her? No, I didn't.

29
00:01:30.483 --> 00:01:33.240
Your turn. Say: No, I didn't.

30
00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.298
No, I didn't.

31
00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:39.132
Base verb.

32
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:43.150
Base verb means the simple form of a verb.

33
00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.448
Eat is the base verb.

34
00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:48.784
Your turn. Say: Base verb.

35
00:01:51.633 --> 00:01:52.867
Base verb.

36
00:01:53.617 --> 00:01:54.722
Yesterday.

37
00:01:55.717 --> 00:01:57.937
Yesterday means the day before today.

38
00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.259
Did you study yesterday?

39
00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.282
Your turn. Say: Yesterday.

40
00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.239
Yesterday.

41
00:02:07.983 --> 00:02:08.833
Ago.

42
00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.977
Ago means back in the past from now.

43
00:02:12.583 --> 00:02:14.188
She left an hour ago.

44
00:02:14.783 --> 00:02:16.960
Your turn. Say: Ago.

45
00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.639
Ago.

46
00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:24.980
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.817 --> 00:02:28.234
Visal, did you watch TV last night?

48
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:41.702
Yes, I did. We make past questions with did + subject + base verb: Did you watch TV? Did she go to school? The verb goes back to its base form.

49
00:02:42.817 --> 00:02:44.526
And negative sentences?

50
00:02:45.617 --> 00:02:54.344
We use didn't + base verb: I didn't eat breakfast. She didn't go to school. Not 'She didn't went', because did already shows the past.

51
00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:56.544
How do we answer?

52
00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:10.637
Use short answers: Yes, I did. No, I didn't. Did he come? Yes, he did. No, he didn't. With question words: What did you eat? Where did she go?

53
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.335
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.183 --> 00:03:19.596
Grammar focus: Past questions and negatives: did and didn't plus base verb.

55
00:03:19.896 --> 00:03:21.141
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:23.954
Did you watch TV last night?

57
00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.699
I didn't eat breakfast this morning.

58
00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:29.200
Where did she go yesterday?

59
00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:39.113
Use did + subject + base verb for questions and didn't + base verb for negatives. After did and didn't, never add -ed or use the past form.

60
00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:43.118
Be careful! Don't say: She didn't went home.

61
00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:47.206
Say: She didn't go home.

62
00:03:47.506 --> 00:03:49.331
Use the base verb after didn't.

63
00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:52.867
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:54.482
Did You…?.

65
00:03:54.782 --> 00:03:57.713
Did you watch TV last night? No, I didn't.

66
00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.943
I didn't watch TV, because I studied.

67
00:04:01.933 --> 00:04:04.504
Did your brother help you? Yes, he did.

68
00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.558
What did you eat for dinner yesterday?

69
00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:11.948
She didn't go to school, because she was ill two days ago.

70
00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:16.954
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:17.817 --> 00:04:19.387
blank you eat breakfast?

72
00:04:19.687 --> 00:04:22.841
A, Do. B, Did. C, Does.

73
00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.005
The answer is B: Did.

74
00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.289
I blank go to school yesterday.

75
00:04:31.589 --> 00:04:34.906
A, didn't. B, don't. C, wasn't.

76
00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.478
The answer is A: didn't.

77
00:04:41.617 --> 00:04:43.456
Did she go? blank

78
00:04:43.756 --> 00:04:48.397
A, Yes, she did.. B, Yes, she went.. C, Yes, she does..

79
00:04:51.933 --> 00:04:53.817
The answer is A: Yes, she did..

80
00:04:54.983 --> 00:04:56.623
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:56.923 --> 00:05:01.703
A, She didn't went home.. B, She didn't go home.. C, She not go home..

82
00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:07.823
The answer is B: She didn't go home..

83
00:05:08.983 --> 00:05:12.202
According to the reading, why didn't the writer watch TV?

84
00:05:12.502 --> 00:05:16.631
A, I studied. B, I was ill. C, I slept.

85
00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:22.027
The answer is A: I studied.

86
00:05:23.233 --> 00:05:26.466
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:27.317 --> 00:05:30.129
Ask a friend one question with 'did' about yesterday.

88
00:05:38.917 --> 00:05:40.498
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:40.798 --> 00:05:53.162
Did you play football yesterday? My friend can answer: Yes, I did, or No, I didn't. I use did with the base verb play, not played. This is the correct way to make a question in the past simple.

90
00:05:53.462 --> 00:05:55.276
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:56.183 --> 00:06:02.725
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past questions and negatives: did and didn't plus base verb.

92
00:06:03.025 --> 00:06:06.954
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

93
00:06:07.254 --> 00:06:09.466
See you in Unit thirty. Goodbye!

94
00:06:09.766 --> 00:06:13.045
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

